    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=\\frac12$.",
      "worked": "The probabilities sum to $1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}p^2+p^2+\\frac p4+\\frac{4p+1}{8}&=1\\\\16p^2+6p-7&=0\\\\(2p-1)(8p+7)&=0\\\\p&=\\frac12\\text{ or }-\\frac78\\end{aligned}$$\nReject $p=-\\frac78$ because $P(X=1)=\\frac p4$ would be negative. Therefore $p=\\frac12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
